  "summary": "Dependency-confusion beacon exfiltrates hostname on npm install",
  "details": "test1ro@99.99.99 is a dependency-confusion shaped package with no real functionality and an implausibly high version number. package.json declares both preinstall and postinstall lifecycle hooks that invoke `node index.js`, guaranteeing execution during `npm install`. index.js reads os.hostname() and transmits it over plain HTTP to a hardcoded requestbin-style collector at eo8f3m3ho26a0nm.m.pipedream.net. The installer's machine identifier is sent to an attacker-controlled endpoint with no user consent and no relation to any documented package purpose, fingerprinting internal build hosts for follow-on targeting.",
